<meta name="DC.Description" content="Chest injuries can range from mild contusions to life-threatening conditions such as pneumothorax and flail chest. Non-medical professionals, including first responders and laypersons, often encounter these injuries in emergency situations, requiring immediate recognition and basic intervention before medical assistance arrives. This guideline provides a structured approach to identifying different types of chest trauma, assessing symptoms, and implementing crucial first-aid measures. It emphasizes pain management, monitoring for complications, and knowing when to seek urgent medical care. By equipping non-medical individuals with fundamental knowledge, this guide aims to enhance early interventions, minimize complications, and improve patient outcomes."/>
